<!--
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0

download-page-snippet.html.tmpl -- template for the site/downloads.html row
(and the two follow-up file edits) for a NEW or RE-PUBLISHED "Postern OS" ISO.

This is a TEMPLATE, not live markup: every {{PLACEHOLDER}} must be filled from
the real values publish-iso.sh prints in its "publish complete" summary, and
the boot-status prose/badge picked to match EXACTLY what -B was published
with -- never round up "QEMU-PENDING" to "boot-validated", never round up
"UNBOOTED" to anything. Do not paste this into site/downloads.html until a
real publish has happened and you have the real SHA-256 in hand.

Three places to update, in this order:

  1. functions/dl/[[path]].js -- add {{NAME}} to the ALLOW set (only needed if
     this is a name not already listed there; publish-iso.sh tells you at the
     end of a run whether this step is required).
  2. site/downloads.html -- the table row below, in the "3 · The reproducible
     OS" section (or a new section/table if this is a genuinely new product
     line, e.g. a cloud-image variant).
  3. Redeploy: ./assemble-public.sh && wrangler pages deploy --branch main
     (per wrangler.toml -- project "posternlabs", pages_build_output_dir=public).

Boot-status -> badge class -> exact prose mapping (do not mix these up):

  UNBOOTED               badge class "proto"   "built · hosted + signed · not yet boot-tested (QEMU or hardware)"
  QEMU-PENDING            badge class "built"   "built · hosted + signed · QEMU boot pending"
  QEMU-PASS:<ev>@<date>   badge class "built"   "built · hosted + signed · QEMU-boot-validated <date> (hardware boot still pending)"
  HARDWARE-BOOTED:<d>@<date> badge class "built" "built · hosted + signed · boots on <device> hardware (<date>)"

QEMU-PASS / HARDWARE-BOOTED additionally require that {{BOOT_EVIDENCE_LINK}}
below actually resolves (the boot log / .evidence sidecar the claim rests on)
-- do not ship the row with a badge implying a boot and a dead evidence link.
-->

<tr>
  <td><strong>{{DISPLAY_NAME}}</strong><br><span class="small dim">{{ARCH}} · {{FIRMWARE}}</span></td>
  <td>{{SIZE_GB}}&nbsp;GB</td>
  <td><span class="badge {{BADGE_CLASS}}">{{BADGE_TEXT}}</span></td>
  <td><a href="/dl/{{NAME}}">Download ISO&nbsp;→</a></td>
  <td><code>{{SHA256}}</code></td>
</tr>

<!--
The shared verify block below this table already covers every row (SHA256SUMS
+ SHA256SUMS.minisig + the minisign pubkey, all under os/v0.1/) -- you do not
need a per-row verify snippet, only the table row above. If {{BOOT_EVIDENCE_LINK}}
is non-empty, add one line to the "Before you install" warnpanel:

    <li><strong>Boot evidence for {{DISPLAY_NAME}}:</strong> <a href="{{BOOT_EVIDENCE_LINK}}">{{BOOT_EVIDENCE_LABEL}}</a> -- {{ONE_LINE_HONEST_CAVEAT}} (e.g. "a QEMU/TCG boot proves the software chain only; it says nothing about real hardware").
-->

<!--
functions/dl/[[path]].js -- ALLOW set edit (only if {{NAME}} is new):

const ALLOW = new Set([
  "postern-os-node-x86_64.iso",
  "postern-os-desktop-x86_64.iso",
  "postern-os-mobile-pinephone-aarch64.img",
  "{{NAME}}",                      // <-- added
]);
-->

